{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin. it stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake as sean parker.\n\nthe film opens with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, getting dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rooney mara). in a fit of anger, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge hit, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark in trouble with the university.\n\nmark is then approached by a group of students, including eduardo saverin and the winklevoss twins, who are interested in creating a social networking site for harvard students. mark agrees to work on the project, but eventually drops the winklevoss twins and starts working on thefacebook with eduardo.\n\nas thefacebook gains popularity, mark and eduardo start to have disagreements over the direction of the site. mark becomes increasingly obsessed with the site and starts to push eduardo out of the company. meanwhile, sean parker, the co-founder of napster, becomes involved with thefacebook and helps mark secure funding from investors.\n\nthe film's narrative is presented through a series of flashbacks, as mark is being sued by eduardo and the winklevoss twins. the film's use of non-linear storytelling is effective in conveying the complexity of the events that unfolded.\n\nthe performances in the film are excellent, with jesse eisenberg delivering a standout performance as mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is also great as eduardo saverin, bringing a sense of vulnerability and desperation to the character. justin timberlake is surprisingly good as sean parker, capturing the character's charisma and arrogance.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy. the music is dark and pulsing, perfectly capturing the mood and atmosphere of the film.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted film that tells a fascinating story. the film's themes of ambition, greed, and betrayal are timely and thought-provoking. the film's use of social media as a backdrop for the story is also effective in exploring the ways in which technology is changing the way we interact with each other.\n\nin conclusion, the social network is a must-see film for anyone interested in the story of facebook or the world of social media. the film's excellent performances, direction, and score make it a compelling and engaging watch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03940728306770325}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.3828373084834311e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.24996495246887207}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.05464606732130051}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.18567566573619843}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -7.152560215217818e-07}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -9.298368240706623e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.218656047465629e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04119579493999481}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.017032857984304428}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00015200339839793742}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0788910835981369}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00016094549209810793}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.08091060072183609}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.11775506287813187}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0017488384619355202}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0036843856796622276}, {"token": ".", "